  "Startup, launch to serving: pocket-engine 1.6-2.5 s (9B) and 5.3 s (27B); vLLM 260 s (9B) and 316 s (27B), including AITER JIT builds and graph compilation.",
  "Accuracy on this GPU (teacher-forced against Transformers bf16, tests/fixtures): 9B bf16 218-219 of 220 picks, misses within one bf16 step, median |dlogprob| 0.0003, p95 0.034; 9B Q4_K_M 210 of 220 (int8 activations), 208 with --no-int8. tests/gpu.rs passes for 9B bf16, 27B bf16 and 9B Q4_K_M.",
  "HIP graphs on ROCm 7.14: greedy 256-token generations of four prompts are identical with and without graphs.",
  "load-hi-* runs 128 then 256 in flight on one server. pocket-engine's second high-load phase on the same server is slower than on a fresh one (load-hi-pe-9b-256-twice-same-server: 3,741 then 2,102 tok/s at 256, median first token 0.20 then 2.25 s) with no KV blocks or slots leaked; under investigation.",
  "vLLM 9B: the burst of 256 failed with a client connection reset (httpx.ReadError) on two attempts; its 128 and 256 closed-loop results stand.",
  "load-pe-9b-q4km-emulated: GGUF before the native int8 MFMA kernel (mma.sync emulated with shuffles). vLLM cannot load Qwen3.5 GGUF files.",
  "--max-batch-tokens 16384 (load-hi-pe-9b-16k-batch-tokens) does not change the 256-in-flight result."
 ]
